module ui.field

// Text fields beyond ui.TextArea, as their own module (`ui.field.<Name>`; `using ui.field` names them bare). Loaded after
// prims (it builds on ui.TextArea) and the tokens.

@tree ChildOf
// A text area that grows with its words to a share of its pane's height (GrowLimit: `share` of the nearest ancestor whose
// height is not its content's, less `keep` points for what the pane shows around it), then scrolls on AppKit's physics.
// When the caret leaves the view (typing, arrows, a paste) it glides back into view, CaretScroll's margin inside the
// edges. The host keeps a harness_native_ui_view::field::FieldScroll per area: it steps it each frame with the caret's
// line and hands it the wheels over the area.
prefab GrowingTextArea : ui.TextArea {
  Size: {w: {kind: Grow, value: 1, min: 0, max: 0}, h: {kind: Fit, value: 0, min: 0, max: 0}}
  GrowLimit: {share: $textarea_grow_share, keep: 0}
  CaretScroll: {margin: $textarea_caret_margin, omega: $textarea_glide_omega, zeta: $textarea_glide_zeta}
}
